  "question": "If $\\vec{a} = 3\\hat{i} - 2\\hat{j} + 4\\hat{k}$ and $\\vec{b} = \\lambda \\hat{i} + 10\\hat{j} + 2\\hat{k}$ are perpendicular, what is the value of $\\lambda$?",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "For perpendicular vectors, $\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b} = 0$.<br /><br />$\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b} = (3)(\\lambda) + (-2)(10) + (4)(2) = 0$<br /><br />$3\\lambda - 20 + 8 = 0$<br /><br />$3\\lambda - 12 = 0$<br /><br />$3\\lambda = 12$<br /><br />$\\lambda = 4$",
